      "common:shortName": [],
      "common:generalComment": [
        {
          "#text": "Polypropylene (PP) is a widely used, recyclable thermoplastic polymer. It is the most commonly used plastic packaging material in the United States due to its melting point and strength. However, PP products degrade slowly in landfills, taking up to 20-30 years to degrade completely. It is used in a range of applications and products, from food packaging to automotive parts, and is known for its strength, durability, and resistance to chemicals and moisture.",
          "@xml:lang": "en"
        },
        {
          "#text": "聚丙烯（PP）是一种广泛使用的可回收热塑性聚合物。由于其熔点和强度，它是美国最常用的塑料包装材料。然而，聚丙烯产品在垃圾填埋场中降解缓慢，需要 20-30 年才能完全降解。从食品包装到汽车零件，聚丙烯被广泛用于各种应用和产品中，并以其强度、耐用性、耐化学性和耐湿性而著称。",
          "@xml:lang": "zh"
        }
      ],
